the signed Builds 6.3.0 release: exact tool pin, range floor, publication handoff, catalog and Builds gitlink. Update the current preparation documentation.\n\nNormal recorded artifact preparation now acquires a private checkout of the bound producer, preserving exact committed catalog bytes despite the producer’s normal CRLF checkout. The final guard rechecks that same producer, and the temporary checkout is removed on exit. Register the real Git regression in the tuple gate.\n\nValidation: tuple/publication/bound-producer, collector/runtime/source controls and source-release tests passed; npm signature audit and commitlint passed. Real public release metadata, NuGet signature, package/executable identity, unchanged owner/source and scratch cleanup passed through the normal artifact-preparation command. The other 17 direct dependency pins are unchanged. Hosted tuple and six SDK gates must pass normally.\n\nStory 2.8 cancellation-order and cleanup qualification remains open; these artifact and source checks grant no native acceptance.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Rebinds the core build/producer tuple, catalog gates, and CI controls that gate Release qualification; changes are mostly pinning and verification, but a bad binding would block the whole pipeline.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Adopts signed Builds 6.3.0** as the current producer tuple: tool pin, range floor `[6.3.0, 7.0.0-0)`, `eng/builds-tuple.json` publication handoff, owner gitlink revisions in `eng/current-tuple-source.json`, and preparation docs.\n> \n> Adds **6.3.0 offline fixtures** and extends **catalog verification** for the new generation (generic SDK **5.2.0**, Tenants **8.0.1**, OpenAPI **3.11.1**, while named SDK4.2 cohorts stay pinned).\n> \n> **Recorded artifact preparation** now materializes a private producer checkout so catalog bytes match the bound release despite CRLF working-tree checkout; the end-to-end guard rechecks that same checkout. Tuple CI runs 